A note from the maintainers
------------------------------------------------------------------------

wa'kijo Community is released under Apache 2.0 — you can use it freely
to build commercial products. We make our money from wa'kijo Pro and
the higher tiers (see https://github.com/benharundev/wa-kijo-pro), which
extend Community with SSO, SCIM, the 11 shared engines, white-labeling,
and other features described in docs/prd.md §8.

Please don't repackage wa'kijo itself as a competing boilerplate product.
The license technically allows it; the community spirit does not. If
you're unsure whether your use case is "building a product with wa'kijo"
(welcome!) or "selling wa'kijo as your own boilerplate" (please don't),
open a discussion at https://github.com/benharundev/wa-kijo/discussions.

